cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Brick DNN in teaching material or in research, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "Brick DNN"
abstract: >-
  A browser-based editor for neural networks and classical machine-learning models: networks
  are built from layers, the shape of every tensor is inferred while building, models are
  trained on the server and exported as readable PyTorch or scikit-learn code.
authors:
  - family-names: "Kühling"
    given-names: "Alexander"
version: "1.1.0"
date-released: "2026-11-09"
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/alexanderKuehling/brick-dnn"
url: "https://brickdnn.com"
keywords:
  - deep learning
  - neural networks
  - PyTorch
  - code generation
  - teaching
